### 4.1 Clone counter — use a Postgres RPC, not a read-then-write from the client
Race-prone to `clones + 1` from the client. Add a `increment_listing_clones(listing_id uuid)` SQL function (`security definer`, owned by a role that can bypass RLS for this one atomic op) in the same migration, and call it via `supabase.rpc('increment_listing_clones', { listing_id })`. This avoids lost updates under concurrent clones.

## 5. Frontend rewiring (data plumbing only, no redesign — same discipline as Phase 10)
- `/app/presets`, `/app/presets/[presetId]`: swap `useWorkspace.myPresets` reads/writes for `lib/presets.ts`, same fetch-with-mock-fallback pattern used everywhere since Phase 10.
- `/app/marketplace/publish/[botId]/page.tsx` (wizard): Step 5 "Publish" button calls `publishPreset()` instead of the local `publishPreset` store action.
- `/app/marketplace`, `/app/marketplace/[presetId]`, public `/marketplace`, `/marketplace/[presetId]`: replace `useMarketplacePresets()` with `listMarketplace()`/`getListing()`. Public pages use the browser Supabase client with no session — confirm `createClient()` works unauthenticated (it will, RLS handles it).
- `/app/creator/dashboard`: replace `publishedPresets`/`CREATOR_EARNINGS` reads with `getMyCreatorStats()`.
- `lib/search-index.ts`: update its preset-indexing source to `listMarketplace()` output instead of the static array — check whether it needs to become async (likely does; audit current sync assumptions).
- Keep `useWorkspace`'s preset state as a post-success cache exactly as established for bots in Phase 10.

## 6. Non-goals
No real payments for `price` (still a display number, no Razorpay — that's Phase 13). No creator payouts. No `/app/compare` changes beyond swapping its data source the same way. No changes to node/graph logic.

## 7. Acceptance checklist
- [ ] `tsc --noEmit` clean.
- [ ] Save/duplicate/delete/rename/restore-version on a private preset all persist across reload, verified in Supabase.
- [ ] Publishing creates a `marketplace_listings` row and it's visible on the **signed-out** `/marketplace` page immediately.
- [ ] Cloning a listing creates an independent preset for the cloning user (editing it never touches the original) and increments `clones` atomically (test two rapid clones, count should be exactly +2).
- [ ] Unpublishing removes it from `/marketplace` but the creator dashboard still shows historical clone/revenue numbers.
- [ ] Reviews: one review per user per listing enforced (unique constraint), rating avg display updates.
- [ ] `/app/compare` and search still work against real marketplace data.


